{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this decision — are you trying to maximize total profit (selling revenue minus feed cost) per animal, or is there a different goal such as maximizing total revenue, minimizing total feed cost, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting multiple options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the numbers of cows, sheep, and chickens required to be whole numbers (you can't raise a fraction of an animal), or is it acceptable to treat them as continuous values for planning purposes?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the variables must be integers or can be continuous."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the feed cost a one-time cost per animal (charged once when you raise it), or is it a recurring daily cost that accumulates over the period the animals are kept?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the timing of feed costs, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any limit on how many cows or sheep you can raise (other than the minimums of 10 and 20 and the total cap of 100 animals), or are cows and sheep unlimited as long as those constraints are met?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether there are additional upper limits on individual animal types beyond the stated minimums and total cap."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the manure constraint a daily limit (i.e., the 800 units per day cap applies to the total manure produced by all animals each day), or is it a one-time total limit over the entire period?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the temporal scope of the manure constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the feed cost is a one-time cost per animal and the manure is a daily limit, is the profit you want to maximize calculated as (selling price - feed cost) per animal, with the manure constraint simply limiting which combinations of animals are feasible each day?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single compound clarification question asking for confirmation of the profit calculation formula and the role of the manure constraint. Since it seeks a single confirmation of the proposed modeling logic, it counts as one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the selling price a one-time revenue per animal (you sell each animal once), or is it a recurring revenue per animal per day?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive revenue models, which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
